Variant prefixes like `md:` only apply to Tailwind utility classes — a plain CSS class defined with `.test { }` isn't one, so `md:test` does nothing. Register it as a real Tailwind utility with `@utility`, then variants work automatically:

```css
@utility test {
  background: red;
}
```
```html
<h3 className="md:test">text</h3>
```

Source: `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, "Adding custom utilities" → "Simple utilities" (lines 402–418).

